# Build output
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# Downloaded SAR scenes and derived products. These are large (tens to hundreds
# of GB) and must never enter git. The directory itself IS tracked, through its
# README: a clone that lacks data/ gives a confusing failure on the first run,
# and the README is now the only tracked record of where the collects come from
# and how to verify one downloaded intact.
data/*
!data/README.md
*.slc
*.cphd
*.SAFE/
*.h5
*.tif
*.tiff
*.pgm

# Intermediate products
out/
*.rsprod

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
compile_commands.json
.cache/


docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

# docs/ is a working area. Only the project's own prose belongs in the
# repository; everything else -- development notes, review transcripts, dataset
# scratch, plans -- is local.
#
# The source papers and the patent are deliberately NOT tracked. They are third-
# party publications, and redistributing them here would mean asserting a
# licence for each one that this project is not in a position to assert. Cite
# them by DOI and publication number instead; a reader can fetch them from the
# publisher. Keeping local copies in docs/ is expected, and is why *.pdf is
# ignored rather than merely untracked.
docs/*
*.pdf
!docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
!docs/USER-GUIDE.md
!docs/DATASETS.md
!docs/IMPLEMENTATION-VERIFICATION.md
!docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md
!docs/CORE-QUESTIONS.md
!docs/FOLLOW-UPS.md

# Synthetic fixtures written into the working tree by the simulator tools.
sim.cphd.truth
sim.cphd
